;ClioSport172.car;My 2002 Clio Sport 172;This car file is not perfect, but should be fun.
;I cheated a bit to improve handling and simulate traction control.
;Hope you like it!
; Valerio
;This file includes describtive comments for most of the parameters.;If you still don't understand a parameter, just leave it unchangend.;these are for the car selection screen;a string with the name of the carcarName "Clio Sport 172"year 2002;displacement in litresdisplacement 2.0

builtIn 1;---aerodynamics;the car's frontal air resistance.;this equals cw*S, where cw is the coefficient of friction ;and S is the frontal area of the car in square meters.;A modern sports car might have values as low as 0.6 for thisfrontAirResistance .8;air resistance of the side and top areas of the car.;these values are not that important to be very exact.sideAirResistance 1.8topAirResistance 2.8;used to simulate spoilers;negative values are downforce, positive values are upforcefrontLift -0.1rearLift -0.1;---chassis;Car's mass in kgmass 1035;Car's momentum of inertia around the x,y and z axis.;Meassured in kg*m^2;For those not into physics that much, inertia specifies the car's;initial resistance to get rotationally accelerated around it's axis. Smaller, lighter;cars have much lower values here. A formula-1 car might have an inertia;around the y-axis af about 750 kg*m^2, whereas a big station wagon may have;4000 kg*m^2. lower values result in better cornering abilitiesinertia {1200,1200,400};The car's center of gravity.;This vector (as all the others that may follow) uses the following;coordinate system: X points to the right, Y points up and Z points to the front.;Coordinates are in meters.;The lower the CG, the better the cars handling.;Also, the further the CG is to the rear of the car, the more the car will tend;to oversteer in corners, making it much harder to handle. If your car uncontrollably;spins out in the rear a lot, try moving the CG further to the front.massCenter {0.0,0.4,.5};An approximation of the car's borders, used for collision detection.;More than two boxes can be used, but if too many are used, performance ;may degrade. Each box is defined by 8 edges (top/front/right to bottom/rear/left).;number of collision boxesnumCollBoxes 2;a list of the collision boxes used, in this case only one;(the vw bus can be aproximated quite well with a single box)# 0coll.tfr {0.859,0.927,1.909}coll.tfl {-0.955,0.927,1.909}coll.trr {0.955,0.927,-1.909}coll.trl {-0.955,0.927,-1.909}coll.bfr {0.955,0.106,1.909}coll.bfl {-0.955,0.106,1.909}coll.brr {0.955,0.106,-1.909}coll.brl {-0.955,0.106,-1.909}

# 1coll.tfr {0.859,1.406,0.279}coll.tfl {-0.955,1.406,0.279}coll.trr {0.955,1.406,-1.570}coll.trl {-0.955,1.406,-1.570}coll.bfr {0.955,0.924,0.279}coll.bfl {-0.955,0.924,0.279}coll.brr {0.955,0.924,-1.570}coll.brl {-0.955,0.924,-1.570};---graphics;Model used to represent the car.model "ClioSport_V057_LR.mdl";Model used to represent the car's interior.;The VW bus has no interior graphics, so we just pass "null.mdl"interiorModel "null.mdl";Position of driver modeldriverPos {0.5,0.6,-0.05};Position of the steering wheelsteeringWheelPos {0.5,0.74,0.414};Angle of the steering wheelsteeringWheelAngle 15;Number of turns, lock-to-lock.steeringWheelTurns 1.5;Model used to represent the steering wheelsteeringWheelModel "null.mdl"

numColors 4# 0colors {0.8,0.8,0.8}# 1colors {0,0,0.5}
# 2colors {0.2,0.2,0.2}# 3colors {0.8,0,0}
;Position of left and right exhaust ends. For a car with only;one exhaust pipe, use the same coordinates for both.exhaust1Pos {0.45,0.2,-1.8}exhaust2Pos {0.45,0.2,-1.8};Position of license plates;for network player namesfrontLicensePlatePos {0,0.36,1.92}rearLicensePlatePos {0,0.8,-1.9};--engine;Car's maximal power in Watts.;One hp equals 745.69987 Watts.power 128260;Car's maximal torque in Nm.;One lb-ft equals 1.35628105 Nm.torque 200;RPM values for the power and torque ratings.powerRPM 6250.0torqueRPM 5400.0;Engines idle RPMidleRPM 800.0jerkRPM 800;RPM delimtermaxRPM 8000.0;Engines Inertia in kg*m^2.;The higher this value is, the longer the engine takes to spin up.engineInertia 0.2;currently unusedengineFriction 100;engine sound sampleengineSample "enginenormal2.wav"hallSample "hallnormal2.wav"zeroRPMSoundGain 0.8fullRPMSoundGain 1.0zeroThrottleSoundGain 0.5fullThrottleSoundGain 1.1zeroRPMSoundPitch 0.4fullRPMSoundPitch 1.5zeroThrottleSoundPitch 0.9fullThrottleSoundPitch 1.0;---suspension;These determines the strength of the car's shock absorbers.supsensionFriction 1500damperStrength 30000;sway Bars will cause the car to tilt less in corners. The higher these values,;the less the car will tilt to the side when corneringfrontSwayBar 15000rearSwayBar 18000;---drivetrain;The ratio of the final drive gear in the car's differential.finalDriveRatio 3.2;The maximum amount of torque the car's clutch can transfer (in Nm).maxClutchTorqueTransfer 800;this factor is used to simulate limited slip differentials.;0 means free differential. the higher the value, the more differential locking.;values around 100 seem to get realistic limited slip differentials.differentialLockCoefficient 0;For automatic transmission: When to shift up and downshiftUpRPM 6000.0shiftDownRPM 4000.0;Time it takes to shift gears in secondsgearSwitchTime 0.2numGears 7# 0gearRatios -3.3# 1gearRatios 0# 2gearRatios 3.5# 3gearRatios 2.4# 4gearRatios 1.9# 5gearRatios 1.6# 6gearRatios 1.12;---wheels;number of wheels (theoretically you could make vehicles with numWheels!=4. This has not been tested and might cause troubles, though).numWheels 4;front left wheel# 0;Wheel's positionwheels.pos {-0.71,0.375,1.2};Wheel's inertia in kg*m^2.wheels.inertia 2.2;Fraction of engine power lead to this wheel.;0, as the bus is rear-wheel drivenwheels.powered 0.4;Friction caused by rotating the wheel in Nm.wheels.friction 10;Maximal steering angle of this wheel in radians.wheels.maxAngle 0.45;Suspension travel of this wheel in meters.wheels.maxSuspension 0.16;Wheel's radius in meters.wheels.radius 0.288;Torque of the brakes on this wheel (in Nm).wheels.braked 5000.0;How much of the braking torque is generated by pulling the handbrake (between 0 and 1).wheels.handbraked 0.0;model used to represent the wheel;we didn't supply a custom model for the wheel, so i'll use one built into the game,wheels.model "cliowheel.mdl";width of the wheel;wider wheels have better grip characteristics.;you might want to use wider wheels at the rear axle if the car tends to oversteer too much.wheels.width 0.195wheels.texture 1;front right wheel# 1wheels.pos {0.71,0.375,1.2}wheels.inertia 2.2wheels.powered 0.4wheels.friction 10wheels.maxAngle 0.45wheels.maxSuspension 0.16wheels.radius 0.288wheels.braked 5000.0wheels.handbraked 0.0wheels.model "cliowheel.mdl"wheels.width 0.195wheels.texture 1;rear left wheel# 2wheels.pos {-0.71,0.375,-1.31}wheels.inertia 2.2wheels.powered 0.1wheels.friction 10wheels.maxAngle 0.0wheels.maxSuspension 0.16wheels.radius 0.288wheels.braked 1800.0wheels.handbraked 1.0wheels.model "cliowheel.mdl"wheels.width 0.195wheels.texture 1;rear right wheel# 3wheels.pos {0.71,0.375,-1.31}wheels.inertia 2.2wheels.powered 0.1wheels.friction 10wheels.maxAngle 0.0wheels.maxSuspension 0.16wheels.radius 0.288wheels.braked 1800.0wheels.handbraked 1.0wheels.model "cliowheel.mdl"wheels.width 0.195wheels.texture 1;---lights;number of lights on the carnumLights 26
# 0;the light's positionlights.pos {-0.61,0.57,1.65};direction the light is pointing tolights.dir {0,-0.1,1};RGB color of the lightlights.rgb {0.5,0.5,1};light type: either 0 for a glowing dot, 1 for a light cone;(visible at night only) or 2 for a dot which reflects on wet streets.lights.type 1;lights size, - length of light cone, or diameter of dotlights.size 30;what is the light used for:;0x01: normal driving light. ;0x08: reverse gear light.;0x10: brake light;0x20: left indicator;0x40: right indicatorlights.onFlags 0x01;tell the light to turn OFF, when one of the above mentioned lights turns on.lights.offFlags 0x00# 1lights.pos {-0.135,1.32,-1.48}lights.dir {0,0,-1}lights.rgb {1,0,0}lights.type 2lights.size 0.035lights.onFlags 0x10lights.offFlags 0x00
